  "applies_to": "WAREMA BACnet 4M230.8I AP surface-mounted controllers (art. 2047 065) driving up to four 230 V blind or venetian blind motors with eight key inputs.",
  "summary": "The 4M230.8I AP is a BACnet MS/TP application specific controller with four two-stage relay outputs for blind motors and eight digital inputs for local UP/DOWN keys. Each blind has a multistate drive command, position and slat angle commands with feedback, and a set of travel-time and slat set-up values. The PICS prints the object layout as per-blind instance ranges.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "1.0",
  "default_device_instance": "1345000 + MS/TP address",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The PICS gives each per-blind object as a range with the blind 1 name (e.g. AV 1-4 \"Blind length 1\" ...). Only the printed blind 1 names are listed; the same objects exist for blinds 2-4 at the next instances: AV 1-4, 5-8, 9-12 ... 53-56 (one per blind), MV 1-4, BV 1-4 and BV 7-10.",
    "BI 1-8 are the external key inputs, printed as \"Input 1 UP\", \"Input 1 DOWN\" ... (UP/DOWN pairs per blind).",
    "The object list also names BV 0, a Group object (group 1, the eight inputs) and two File objects (configuration and update); BV 0 has no description and is not listed.",
    "Access is from the Present_Value column: RW-V (volatile) for the commands, RW-N (stored in flash) for set-up values; shown here as W.",
    "Source: PICS sections 2-5 and 8, pages 4-9."
  ],
